WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.870
Central Ops Travel helps verified ShipHero employees coordinate customer onsite visits. Sign in with your ShipHero Google account to submit requests, view the map, or join a trip.

2
00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:21.310
Open Requests, choose the visit type and date confidence, then add the customer name, customer link, warehouse address, dates, point of contact, and warehouse start time.

3
00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:29.820
For an onboarding onsite, answer every readiness question. A No answer is allowed. The checklist helps the team understand what still needs attention before the visit.

4
00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:39.860
Submit the request. The approval and assignment steps happen behind the scenes. Once approved, the engagement appears in the upcoming travel list and on the shared C S Onsite Google Calendar.

5
00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:48.180
Use Map View to see when and where approved engagements are happening. Open a visit and choose Join and shadow. The Calendar invitation updates with the right people.

6
00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:57.450
If plans change, the original requester can request new dates or cancellation. Those changes return for approval, then the Calendar and attendees update automatically.

7
00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:06.390
Use Central Ops Travel to keep requests, travelers, and Calendar invitations aligned. Start your next request with a verified ShipHero email address.
